<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Eggenberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Eggenberg was an Austrian noble family from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/graz">Graz</a> that rose to great wealth in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> service. Hans Ulrich von Eggenberg, chief adviser of Emperor Ferdinand II, was made a prince and received the Bohemian duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesky-krumlov">Krumau</a>. The family built Eggenberg Palace in Graz; when its male line died out in 1717, its Bohemian estates passed to the Schwarzenbergs.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-eggenberg.jpg" alt="House of Eggenberg" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_Eggenberg_(ancient).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
